@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
autonumber
title Check Out and Receipt Settlement
actor Operator
boundary "REST endpoints" as API
control "Operations and billing services" as S
database PostgreSQL as DB
Operator -> API : POST /api/parking/check-out/\nregistration_number
API -> API : Authenticate and validate operator request
API -> S : check_out_vehicle(...)
activate S
group Checkout atomic transaction
 S -> DB : Lock vehicle active record and slot
 alt No active session
  S --> API : 404 Not Found
 else Active session
  S -> DB : Read vehicle class tariff
  S -> S : Apply inclusive grace and hourly rounding\nUse Decimal arithmetic
  S -> DB : Save fee and tariff snapshots\nComplete record and release slot
  alt Persistence or release error
   DB --> S : Roll back all checkout changes
  else Successful commit
   DB --> S : Completed record
  end
 end
end
S --> API : Completed record or structured error
deactivate S
API --> Operator : 200 fee details or error status
opt Checkout completed
Operator -> API : POST /api/parking/receipts/\nrecord_id
API -> S : Generate or retrieve receipt
S -> DB : Read completed fee snapshots\nCreate unique receipt if absent
DB --> S : Receipt and payment status
S --> API : Receipt
API --> Operator : 201 Created or 200 existing
Operator -> API : POST /api/parking/receipts/{uuid}/payment/\nstatus method amount
group Settlement atomic transaction
 API -> S : Validate role amount and transition
 S -> DB : Lock receipt and completed session\nUpdate payment mirrors and audit
 DB --> S : Commit settlement together
end
S --> API : Updated receipt
API --> Operator : 200 payment confirmation
end
note over Operator, DB
Checkout receipt generation and settlement are separate API operations.
Repeating the same receipt or settlement request is idempotent.
end note
@enduml
